      "key": "panelF196635A81E92A4B",
      "title": "Untitled (Copy)",
      "visualSettings": "{\"general\":{\"mode\":\"TextPanel\",\"type\":\"text\",\"displayType\":\"default\"},\"title\":{\"fontSize\":14},\"series\":{},\"legend\":{\"enabled\":false},\"text\":{\"showTitle\":false,\"horizontalAlignment\":\"left\"}}",
      "keepVisualSettingsConsistentWithParent": true,
      "panelType": "TextPanel",
      "text": "Bans Lurker\n#####The ban lurker is a feature of Varnish that can help you keep a clean cache, by scaring seldom-accessed objects with long TTLs out into the open. Here they can be executed humanly by Varnish's flexible ban-purging mechanism. These objects would otherwise hide in the corners until their TTLs expired."
